## ✍ DM Response
In response to Emmett's action, he presses his ear against the crack in the sealed door of Aldwick Mine, listening intently for the shape of the silence coming through. The air near the crack feels oddly warm and still, almost as if it is alive with an unseen energy.

As Emmett listens, he senses a faint echo of a sound that is not quite a sound, a distant drumbeat almost lost in the background noise of his own heartbeat. It's a feeling he's familiar with — a presence from beyond the veil of the living world. The silence seems to pulse with a rhythm that matches the beat of his own heart, as if it is trying to communicate with him.

Suddenly, the drumbeat grows louder and more insistent, filling Emmett's ears and making his heart race. He feels a wave of dread wash over him, an icy chill that sends shivers down his spine. The silence seems to be reaching out to him, trying to pull him deeper into itself.

Emmett struggles to maintain his composure as the drumbeat reaches a crescendo, drowning out all other sounds and leaving him disoriented and disoriented. He knows he has been counted by something powerful and malevolent, and he feels a sudden urge to run, to escape from whatever is lurking beyond that sealed door.

But before he can act on his impulse, the drumbeat suddenly fades away, leaving him alone in the cold, dark chamber of Aldwick Mine. He takes a deep breath, trying to calm himself and banish the feeling of dread that has settled over him. He knows he cannot afford to let fear control him, not if he wants to survive this investigation.

As he stands there, listening to the silence once more, Emmett feels a new presence enter the chamber. It's a woman's voice, soft and trembling with fear. "Emmett Grave," she whispers, her voice barely audible over the sound of the rain outside. "You have been counted. And I warn you — do not let it learn your shape."

The voice disappears as suddenly as it appeared, leaving Emmett standing alone in the darkness once more. He knows he has made a powerful enemy, but he also knows that he cannot turn back now. He has come too far to give up now, and he will do whatever it takes to uncover the truth about what lies beneath Aldwick Mine.

But as he turns to leave the chamber, Emmett feels a new wave of dread wash over him. He knows that whatever is down there, it is not something to be trifled with. And he can't shake the feeling that he may have already made a grave mistake in coming here.

